==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*varis}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*warᴈ}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|vares}}, {{cog|vep|variš}}, {{cog|krl|varoi}} and {{cog|hu|varjú}}. Likely an onomatopoeic word, compare {{noncog|ru|ворона}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[hooded crow]], [[grey crow]], ''[[Corvus cornix]]''
# [[corvid]], [[crow]] {{gloss|any bird of the genus ''Corvus''}}

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-vastaus|vari|a}}

====Usage notes====
Until recently [[carrion crow]] (''[[nokivaris]]'', which is rarely seen in Finland but common in England) was believed to be just a black variant of [[hooded crow]] or [[grey crow]] (which is common in Finland but less common in England). Therefore many dictionaries give "carrion crow" as translation for '''''varis'''''.

